cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Quantum-biology demos: a governed quantum pipeline and a bioprocess yardstick"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Chernov
    given-names: Alexander
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-3198-2712"
repository-code: "https://github.com/doytsujin/ok-quantum-biology-demos"
abstract: >-
  Two small, runnable demonstrations of placing a computational step inside a
  governed biology workflow. The first reproduces QuASeR's de novo assembly as
  QAOA on PennyLane (three reads, nine qubits, verified against brute force),
  trains a variational quantum classifier downstream of it, and places both
  behind a dataset-descriptor runtime and a gateway with admission control,
  rate limiting, a circuit-identity cache and an event record. The second is a
  mechanistic fed-batch CHO bioreactor model under a contract of in-process
  limits, with a search controller that chooses a feed plan and writes an
  attributed decision artifact. Neither claims quantum advantage; every
  instance is small enough to check classically, and each is checked.
keywords:
  - quantum computing
  - QAOA
  - variational quantum classifier
  - PennyLane
  - de novo assembly
  - bioprocess
  - CHO cell culture
  - admission control
  - provenance
